From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathias Fredriksson <mafredri@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:34:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] ICP: AES_GCM: Make DEBUG_GCM_ASM opt-in

DEBUG_GCM_ASM was defined in every DEBUG build. It shadows each AVX
context with an SSE one, and the SSE init asserts on IVs other than 12
bytes, so crypto_test aborts in --enable-debug builds. ZTS runs it in
icp_aes_gcm, and CI builds with --enable-debug. Leave the define for
developers to set.

Signed-off-by: Mathias Fredriksson <mafredri@gmail.com>
---
 module/icp/include/modes/modes.h | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/module/icp/include/modes/modes.h b/module/icp/include/modes/modes.h
index da8f60d69635..c964a5476884 100644
--- a/module/icp/include/modes/modes.h
+++ b/module/icp/include/modes/modes.h
@@ -43,10 +43,11 @@ extern "C" {
 /* XXXX: does AES + PCLMULQDQ really imply at least SSE4_1? */
 #define	CAN_USE_GCM_ASM
 
-#ifdef DEBUG
-/* Defines this to the gcm_simd_impl_t to debug. */
-#define	DEBUG_GCM_ASM	GSI_ISALC_SSE
-#endif
+/*
+ * Define DEBUG_GCM_ASM to a gcm_simd_impl_t, e.g. GSI_ISALC_SSE, to run that
+ * implementation on a shadow copy of every AVX context and log differences.
+ * It asserts on IVs other than 12 bytes, which crypto_test's vectors use.
+ */
 #if defined(HAVE_SSE4_1)
 #define	CAN_USE_GCM_ASM_SSE
 #endif
